From c67e01a240e919c6a7fc98a6c88462ac0b053e72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:29:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban pickup-stall: read the registry hold by
 truthiness, like pickup's eligible()

Problem: the pickup-stall alarm modules counted a machine as held only when the registry's `hold` was
exactly `True` (`kanban_pickup_stall.expected_hold`, `kanban_pickup_stall_held.stranded`,
`kanban_pickup_stall_resolve._hold_lifted`), while pickup's `kanban_worker_node.eligible()` and the
placement readers (`kanban_placement*`, `kanban_move`, `kanban_runs_on_capabilities`) hold on any truthy
`hold`. A non-bool truthy value (e.g. "yes", "1") made pickup record `hold` skips while the alarm read the
hold as lifted: no hold repair was filed, and the resolve sweep would close an open one as `hold_lifted`.
Latent only (the Board writes a bool today); review nit 1 of PR #2439 (t_01a1d5edccfabef8).

Fix: the three readers use `not entry.get("hold")` / `entry.get("hold")`, so lifted = readable entry with no
truthy hold. An unreadable registry still fails toward alerting (unchanged).

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_stall_lifted.py adds
- test_a_non_bool_truthy_hold_is_held_like_pickup_reads_it: hold="yes" files the hold repair and a later
  sweep leaves it ready (no "lifted" note).
- test_expected_hold_reads_a_non_bool_truthy_hold_as_held: hold="1" inside a rollout window is expected;
  hold="" is not.
RED on main (both fail: no repair filed / expected_hold None); GREEN with the fix: 234 tests across every
test file importing kanban_pickup_stall pass.
